function DEFS(){var mt=D.meta;return '<h2>Definitions & data limits</h2><p class="note">Data as of <b>'+esc(mt.asof_label)+'</b>. Refreshed roughly every 30 minutes Mon–Sat 6 AM–7:30 PM ET.</p>'+
'<h3>Sales data this month (top section)</h3><p>Current calendar month only (Oct 1 → today); not affected by the window toggle. <b>Sold</b> = Sold (Final) <b>plus Sold (Designer), shown as “pending Final”</b> (designer marked it sold; it almost always becomes a sale). Final-only and pending are always shown separately. Pending deals are dated by the Designer Sold Date when present, otherwise the date the stage last changed to Sold (Designer); their CloseDate field is a placeholder and is not used. This applies to every sold total, chart, trend, designer row and funnel on the board. <b>Official close rate stays Sold (Final) ÷ held first appointments</b>; an “incl. designer-sold” rate is shown beside it for reference. The 17 Lowe\'s bay records stay excluded. <b>Month pace</b> = straight-line share of the Q4 target: Q4 target × days in month ÷ 92, pace today = month target × day-of-month ÷ days in month (simple and even; real sales are lumpy). <b>Appointments held</b> = first appointments dated this month through today that were not cancelled or no-show. <b>Quotes issued</b> = opportunities with an appointment this month through today, held (or sold), with a $ amount > 0 (quote date is not stored; the quote is made at the appointment) — includes quotes since sold or lost. <b>Quoted, still open</b> = those still in a working stage. <b>Leads</b> = Lead records created this month in the NJ designer territory. <b>Close rate MTD</b> uses the corporate and lead-basis methods below; MTD rates run low because recent appointments have not had time to close. <b>Last month comparison</b> = previous month, day 1 through the same day-of-month (sold by sale date, everything else by appointment/created date), plus the full previous month. Designers: sold by Assigned Designer (else owner); non-roster owners roll into one "Other" row so totals tie.</p>'+
pcDefs()+'<h3>Month focus: path to goal</h3>'+(D.focus?'<p class="note">Data as of <b>'+esc(D.focus.asof)+'</b></p><ul>'+D.focus.method.map(function(x){return '<li>'+esc(x)+'</li>'}).join('')+'</ul>':'')+'<h3>Sales progression by month</h3><p>One line per month of 2026: cumulative <b>Sold (Final) $</b> by day of month, by sale (close) date, NJ only, the 17 Lowe\'s bay placeholder records excluded, and nothing dated after today. The current month is drawn only through today. Completed months are final. <b>Day 10 / day 20</b> = share of the month\'s final total sold through that day; <b>Last 10</b> = share sold in the last 10 calendar days of the month. <b>Fast starter</b> = ≥30% of the month sold by day 10; <b>Back-loaded</b> = ≥40% sold in the last 10 days; otherwise <b>Balanced</b> (an even pace would be about 32% / 32%). <b>Typical month</b> = the median across completed months for each day. In the % view completed months are % of their own final; the current month is shown as % of the typical (median) month total because its own final is not known yet. The implied month-end is today\'s total ÷ the typical share closed by this day, with a range from the fastest- to slowest-starting completed month. It is a pattern comparison, not a forecast; today may be a partial day. All numbers are pre-computed in refresh.py.</p>'+
'<h3>Database window (30 / 45 / 60 / 90 days / All open)</h3><p>The toggle sets the window for pipeline by stage and source, aging heatmap, deal health tiers, overlooked items, at-risk list, funnel and designer rows. <b>Window = deal age by first appointment date</b> (days since the first appointment; if no appointment, since the opportunity was created). Quote date and last-activity date are not used: quote date is not stored, and last activity would let touched-but-stale deals look recent. A deal is <b>inside</b> a window when that age ≤ N days (future appointments count as inside); older open deals are <b>outside</b> and still shown as "outside $" / dormant so the big picture is not lost. <b>All open</b> = every open working deal. Default is 45 days. For the funnel and designer sold/close columns the same window is applied to appointment dates and sale dates in the last N days (All open → YTD). The no-show/cancelled overlooked list uses the last N days (All open → 90 days). "New" stage (booked, not worked) is not window-limited. Deal health tiers are the same definitions inside every window (dormant requires 90+ days, so it only appears under All open).</p>'+
'<h3>Scope</h3><p>New Jersey only: Opportunities with CompanySettings = Closet Factory NJ; Leads in the "New Jersey – Designers" service territory. Read-only from ClosetWare.</p>'+
'<h3>Close rate (corporate)</h3><p>Sold (Final) counted by sale (close) date, including designer-created and no-appointment sales, ÷ held first appointments (Net Lead) by appointment date. The 17 Lowe\'s "In Store Bay" placeholder records marked Sold (Final) with no value (16 on Jul 21, 1 on Aug 6) are excluded.</p>'+
'<h3>Lead-basis rate (secondary)</h3><p>Logged appointments only, lead-sourced (excludes repeat, walk-in, designer-created): sold ÷ held-or-sold first appointments. Normally lower than corporate because it ignores sales with no logged appointment.</p>'+
'<h3>Sold $</h3><p>Opportunity Amount of Sold (Final) plus Sold (Designer, pending Final) by sale date (see month section note). Q4 target $3,569,335 (Oct 1–Dec 31, 2026), straight-line pace.</p>'+
'<h3>Open pipeline / quotes</h3><p>Working stages: Current, Second 1-7, Last 8-14, Aging 14+, Future Sale, Manager Review. "New" = booked, not yet worked (shown separately). Quote $ = Opportunity Amount.</p>'+
'<h3>Stale / at risk</h3><p>Stale = no plan-to-close update (non-office edit in field history, or a dated entry in the notes) in 14+ days. Next step = future follow-up date, future appointment, open task, or a future date written in the notes. At risk = stale AND no next step. Dormant = at risk with appointment 90+ days ago. Healthy = neither.</p>'+
'<h3>Designers</h3><p>Attribution = Assigned Designer, else opportunity owner. Designers do not set appointments (the office does), so lead response speed is not shown as a designer metric. Rates are colored only with 20+ first appts: green ≥3 pts above team, red ≥3 below. † marks rates inflated by no-appointment/designer-created sales.</p>'+
'<h3>Limits</h3><ul><li>Deals are identified by client first name, designer, amount and stage. Only first names shown; no phones, emails or full names.</li><li>Notes are parsed locally for dates only; poorly formatted notes can understate activity.</li><li>Cancelled/no-show opps are closed Lost and carry no $; open deals have no cancellation history. E-signature fields are not populated, so "contract out" cannot be tracked.</li><li>Lead counts are Lead records; not matched 1:1 to appointments in the same period.</li><li>Straight-line Q4 pace ignores seasonality.</li><li>Prior-year comparisons omitted: 2025 history in this pull is incomplete.</li></ul>'}
